  "interpretation": "<h3 data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1051\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1051\">Method:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1237\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1117\">\n<p data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1117\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1054\" data-end=\"1087\">Surface electrode stimulation</strong> of <strong data-start=\"1091\" data-end=\"1117\">posterior tibial nerve</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1181\">\n<p data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1181\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\">Recording from <strong data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1155\">scalp electrodes</strong> over somatosensory cortex</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1237\">\n<p data-start=\"1184\" data-end=\"1237\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\">Signal averaging used for accurate waveform detection</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start=\"1244\" data-end=\"1285\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1251\" data-end=\"1285\">Clinical Use / Interpretation:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1589\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1336\">\n<p data-start=\"1288\" data-end=\"1336\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\">Assesses <strong data-start=\"1297\" data-end=\"1336\">integrity of somatosensory pathways</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1337\" data-end=\"1484\">\n<p data-start=\"1339\" data-end=\"1375\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\">Used in diagnosis and monitoring of:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1378\" data-end=\"1484\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1378\" data-end=\"1402\">\n<p data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1402\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1380\" data-end=\"1402\">Multiple sclerosis</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1405\" data-end=\"1431\">\n<p data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1431\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1431\">Spinal cord injuries</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1434\" data-end=\"1463\">\n<p data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1463\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1463\">Peripheral neuropathies</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1484\">\n<p data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1484\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1484\">Myelopathies</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\" data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1589\">\n<p data-start=\"1487\" data-end=\"1589\"><span style=\"font-size: 9.38px;\"><strong data-start=\"1487\" data-end=\"1508\">Prolonged latency</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1533\">reduced amplitude</strong> may indicate <strong data-start=\"1547\" data-end=\"1589\">neural conduction delay or dysfunction</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
